---
title: Border effects
description: Four, and they are the system's own line work. The design language here is the ruled grid — hairlines, registration marks, rulers — so an edge is drawn the same way. Nothing glows; nothing is a rainbow.
eyebrow: Effects
source: src/effects/border.css
---
<h2>Corners</h2>
<p>Four brackets instead of a box — the mark a designer puts round something to say <em>this</em>. With <code>im-fx-corners-close</code> they run along the edges on hover until they meet: the same gesture as a card's edge sharpening.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-fit" style="--im-grid-min: 15rem; --im-grid-gap: 1.5rem">
	<div class="im-fx-corners p-6"><p class="im-caption" data-index="01">im-fx-corners</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm">Brackets, at rest.</p></div>
	<a class="im-fx-corners im-fx-corners-close block p-6 no-underline" href="#corners"><p class="im-caption" data-index="02">-close</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body">Hover: the brackets close into a frame.</p></a>
	<figure class="im-fx-corners im-fx-corners-close p-2" style="--im-fx-ink: var(--im-accent); --im-fx-length: 1.25rem; --im-fx-width: 2px"><img class="block w-full" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; object-fit: cover" src="{{demo.post.feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Ticks</h2>
<p>A ruler along an edge: minor ticks every half rem, major every 2.5. The same ruler as the <a href="/layout/divider/#the-ruler">divider</a>.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-fit" style="--im-grid-min: 15rem; --im-grid-gap: 1.5rem">
	<div class="im-fx-ticks ring-line px-6 pb-6"><p class="im-caption" data-index="cm">im-fx-ticks</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm">Along the top.</p></div>
	<div class="im-fx-ticks im-fx-ticks-bottom ring-line px-6 pt-6"><p class="im-caption">-bottom</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm">Along the bottom.</p></div>
	<div class="im-fx-ticks im-fx-ticks-left ring-line py-6 pr-6" style="--im-fx-ink: var(--im-accent)"><p class="im-caption">-left, in the accent</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm">Down the side.</p></div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Trace</h2>
<p>A hairline box with one bright segment travelling round it — a scanner, a "live" state, the one plan in a pricing row you want looked at first. <strong>One per view</strong>; it never stops moving.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-fit" style="--im-grid-min: 15rem; --im-grid-gap: 1.5rem">
	<div class="im-fx-trace rounded-xl p-6"><p class="im-caption" data-index="●">im-fx-trace</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm">The accent travels the rule.</p></div>
	<div class="im-fx-trace rounded-xl p-6" style="--im-fx-ink: var(--im-ink); --im-fx-speed: 3s"><p class="im-caption">In ink, faster</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm"><code>--im-fx-ink</code>, <code>--im-fx-speed</code>.</p></div>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p>It paints the border with a second background, so the box keeps a solid fill — set <code>--im-fx-bg</code> if it is not on the page canvas. Where a browser cannot animate the angle, it is a still hairline.</p>

<h2>Draw</h2>
<p>The rule draws itself round the box on hover — from the top-left and the bottom-right at once.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-fit" style="--im-grid-min: 15rem; --im-grid-gap: 1.5rem">
	<a class="im-fx-draw block p-6 no-underline" href="#draw"><p class="im-caption">im-fx-draw</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body">From nothing.</p></a>
	<a class="im-fx-draw ring-line block p-6 no-underline" href="#draw" style="--im-fx-ink: var(--im-accent)"><p class="im-caption">Over a hairline</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body">The accent is drawn over a resting rule.</p></a>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>On components</h2>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-fit" style="--im-grid-min: 15rem; --im-grid-gap: 1.5rem">
	<a class="im-card im-card-plain im-fx-corners im-fx-corners-close p-5" href="#on-components"><span class="im-card-title">A quiet card</span><span>Brackets, no surface.</span><span class="im-card-cta">Read {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</span></a>
	<div class="im-card im-card-plain im-fx-trace p-5" style="border-radius: var(--im-radius-xl)"><span class="im-badge im-badge-accent" style="align-self: start">Pro</span><span class="im-card-title">The plan to look at</span><span>Trace, on the one card that should be seen first.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell im-fx-ticks ring-line"><p class="im-caption" data-index="03">A measured cell</p><span>Ticks on a Swiss cell.</span></div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Variables</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>--im-fx-ink</code></td><td>The line's colour. Ink by default; the accent for trace.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-fx-width</code></td><td>Its thickness. 1–1.5px.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-fx-length</code></td><td>Corners: how long each bracket arm is. 0.875rem.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-fx-speed</code></td><td>Trace: one lap. 5s.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Earlier versions also had gradient, glow, marching-dash and offset borders. They looked like a different product, so they were removed; the marching dashes live on where they mean something — the <a href="/forms/controls/#file-drop">file drop</a>.</p>
